01:01:08.519 --> 01:01:09.779
- Because sometimes when you have,

01:01:09.779 --> 01:01:14.036
as much as I love tsukemen,
it's like Five Guys, right?

01:01:14.036 --> 01:01:16.209
It's like, man, this
flavor is so powerful,

01:01:16.209 --> 01:01:17.997
it sticks to me the entire time,

01:01:17.997 --> 01:01:19.712
but then the moment it starts to settle

01:01:19.712 --> 01:01:22.073
in your stomach, you're
just like "Kill me!"

01:01:22.073 --> 01:01:23.767
- Five Guys is that thing
where you're just like,

01:01:23.767 --> 01:01:25.772
"I'm out for the count
for the rest of the day.

01:01:25.772 --> 01:01:28.064
Don't talk to me, don't
expect me to do anything."

01:01:28.064 --> 01:01:29.804
- I never thought food could knock you out

01:01:29.804 --> 01:01:31.468
until I had Five Guys.

01:01:31.468 --> 01:01:34.713
- The opposite of that I
feel is sushi and sashimi.

01:01:34.713 --> 01:01:36.689
I also had no fucking
clue what sashimi was

01:01:36.689 --> 01:01:37.765
until I first came here.

01:01:37.765 --> 01:01:38.886
- A lot of people don't.
- Seriously?

01:01:38.886 --> 01:01:39.950
- No, seriously.

01:01:39.950 --> 01:01:40.858
- A lot of people don't.

01:01:40.858 --> 01:01:42.236
- 'Cause I didn't know
if there was a choice

01:01:42.236 --> 01:01:43.998
where you could just get rid of the rice.

01:01:43.998 --> 01:01:46.864
(laughing)

01:01:46.864 --> 01:01:49.394
I guess it's like a
steak without the sides.

01:01:49.394 --> 01:01:51.402
Like you could just have a steak,

01:01:51.402 --> 01:01:54.819
and I thought, oh, I mean, yeah, I guess.

01:01:55.808 --> 01:01:57.768
I will admit, I wanted to be that guy

01:01:57.768 --> 01:02:00.277
who immediately loved sashimi
and sushi and was like,

01:02:00.277 --> 01:02:02.100
"Dude, I fucking love this."

01:02:02.100 --> 01:02:03.480
But it took me a while to get used to it

01:02:03.480 --> 01:02:06.803
and really get into it and
appreciate the taste of it.

01:02:06.803 --> 01:02:09.801
Because when I first
had sashimi, I'm like,

01:02:09.801 --> 01:02:10.634
"Yeah, it doesn't taste good."

01:02:10.634 --> 01:02:11.467
- Really?

01:02:11.467 --> 01:02:12.300
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:02:12.300 --> 01:02:14.017
- It was definitely
something that grew on me,

01:02:14.017 --> 01:02:17.384
'cause I remember I went most
of my childhood hating sushi

01:02:17.384 --> 01:02:19.709
and hating sashimi 'cause I was like

01:02:19.709 --> 01:02:21.688
"Raw fish? Why do I wanna eat raw stuff?"

01:02:21.688 --> 01:02:24.016
- And in the UK, they
do that shit dirty, bro.

01:02:24.016 --> 01:02:25.397
Your sushi sucks dick.

01:02:25.397 --> 01:02:26.230
(laughing)

01:02:26.230 --> 01:02:27.757
- True.
- Fucking awful.

01:02:27.757 --> 01:02:29.892
- I had this one day where I just,

01:02:29.892 --> 01:02:32.134
for some reason I was like,

01:02:32.134 --> 01:02:34.080
"Man, that kinda looks appetizing.

01:02:34.080 --> 01:02:35.841
Let me, let me give that shot."

01:02:35.841 --> 01:02:38.829
And then after the first
time when I was an adult

01:02:38.829 --> 01:02:40.709
and I tried sushi again I was like,

01:02:40.709 --> 01:02:41.880
"I fucking love this shit."

01:02:41.880 --> 01:02:44.092
I love the taste of raw
fish, tastes amazing.

01:02:44.092 --> 01:02:47.555
And having sushi in
Japan is just the quality

01:02:47.555 --> 01:02:50.265
of the fish is just so damn good

01:02:50.265 --> 01:02:53.259
that even if you go to
one of those dollar places

01:02:53.259 --> 01:02:58.259
where you can order a small
plate of sushi for a dollar,

01:02:58.679 --> 01:03:00.602
that still tastes way better than some

01:03:00.602 --> 01:03:02.957
of the best restaurants
that you can find in the UK

01:03:02.957 --> 01:03:03.790
or something like that.

01:03:03.790 --> 01:03:04.668
- Yeah, it's true.

01:03:04.668 --> 01:03:06.857
I mean, the quality of like,

01:03:06.857 --> 01:03:08.442
because most of the fish that they serve,

01:03:08.442 --> 01:03:09.894
we obviously don't have in the UK,

01:03:09.894 --> 01:03:12.027
but even when you get
the salmon, you're like,

01:03:12.027 --> 01:03:13.863
"Holy shit, I didn't know salmon

01:03:13.863 --> 01:03:16.214
could just fall apart like
this when you bite into it."

01:03:16.214 --> 01:03:17.756
Normally in the UK, you know,
you get something salmon,

01:03:17.756 --> 01:03:19.822
you gotta fucking tug away.

01:03:19.822 --> 01:03:21.669
- You gotta Bear Grylls that shit.

01:03:21.669 --> 01:03:24.515
- I've had salmon where
I'm literally fucking,

01:03:24.515 --> 01:03:25.620
trying to sever it.

01:03:25.620 --> 01:03:28.086
But in Japan, you eat it
and it just falls apart,

01:03:28.086 --> 01:03:29.961
and it works so good with the rice,

01:03:29.961 --> 01:03:32.863
But man, if I ever have a workout,

01:03:32.863 --> 01:03:34.207
sushi is what I'm always craving.

01:03:34.207 --> 01:03:35.967
It's the best post-workout meal, I think.

01:03:35.967 --> 01:03:36.800
- Really?

01:03:36.800 --> 01:03:38.836
- 'Cause it's like it's
just filling enough

01:03:38.836 --> 01:03:40.016
where it's like I don't wanna go too hard,

01:03:40.016 --> 01:03:41.494
but so healthy and so good for you,

01:03:41.494 --> 01:03:44.116
You're like, "Man, I really,
I feel healthy doing this."

01:03:44.116 --> 01:03:45.172
- But I remember you were once saying

01:03:45.172 --> 01:03:48.365
that you can't have sushi for dinner.

01:03:48.365 --> 01:03:50.253
Which is weird because
I'll take any excuse

01:03:50.253 --> 01:03:52.148
to take sushi for dinner.
- Yeah, same here, same here.

01:03:52.148 --> 01:03:54.061
- Yeah, whenever these guys
when we're out, they're like,

01:03:54.061 --> 01:03:54.977
"You guys wanna get sushi for dinner?"

01:03:54.977 --> 01:03:55.832
I'm like-

01:03:55.832 --> 01:03:57.326
- No, no, it's always "What
do you guys wanna eat?"

01:03:57.326 --> 01:03:59.317
And Connor's like, "I'm easy."

01:03:59.317 --> 01:04:00.809
And I go, "Do you feel like sushi?"

01:04:00.809 --> 01:04:02.127
- No sushi.
- No, no don't want sushi.

01:04:02.127 --> 01:04:02.960
- Then you're not easy.
(laughing)

01:04:02.960 --> 01:04:05.404
- You are not!
- That is not easy!

01:04:05.404 --> 01:04:07.084
- That was a fucking lie!

01:04:07.084 --> 01:04:09.641
- It's like, okay, I'm easy.

01:04:09.641 --> 01:04:11.783
If you wanna go to sushi, we'll go sushi.

01:04:11.783 --> 01:04:15.080
I'm just gonna be like,
"It's not it, chief."

01:04:15.080 --> 01:04:16.316
- Well, then we don't wanna
do that to you, right?

01:04:16.316 --> 01:04:18.034
- For dinner, 'cause
for dinner I feel like,

01:04:18.034 --> 01:04:20.054
okay, sushi is great, don't get me wrong.

01:04:20.054 --> 01:04:24.373
But for lunch, I don't
mind having one flavor.

01:04:24.373 --> 01:04:27.334
But for sushi I feel
like 'cause it all tastes

01:04:27.334 --> 01:04:29.206
like fish still at the end of the day;

01:04:29.206 --> 01:04:31.275
yes, the fish are different
and they taste different,

01:04:31.275 --> 01:04:34.236
but it still feels I'm
just eating fish and rice

01:04:34.236 --> 01:04:36.742
Which is fine, but for some
reason it's sushi to me,

01:04:36.742 --> 01:04:38.282
it doesn't feel like a full meal.

01:04:38.282 --> 01:04:39.502
- But you know you can get-

01:04:39.502 --> 01:04:40.853
- Other stuff, I know.

01:04:40.853 --> 01:04:43.350
But like, when you order fried
chicken at a sushi place,

01:04:43.350 --> 01:04:45.766
that shit is so fucking awful.

01:04:45.766 --> 01:04:49.729
It's like the fucking chicken
has been abused and beaten up.

01:04:49.729 --> 01:04:51.160
It's all muscular and shit,

01:04:51.160 --> 01:04:53.729
like it's been in a fucking
fight club before it was killed.

01:04:53.729 --> 01:04:55.659
You maybe get one ounce of chicken breast

01:04:55.659 --> 01:04:58.397
and the rest is this
black bone with veins.

01:04:58.397 --> 01:05:00.939
You're like, "Holy shit, what
did they do to this chicken?"

01:05:00.939 --> 01:05:02.611
And then you're like, what's the point?

01:05:02.611 --> 01:05:03.936
- It's like 'roided up chicken.

01:05:03.936 --> 01:05:06.819
- Yeah, yeah, and I'm
hitting up the miso soup

01:05:06.819 --> 01:05:09.107
like no tomorrow and I'm stocking up on it

01:05:09.107 --> 01:05:10.238
'cause it's normally free.

01:05:10.238 --> 01:05:12.761
Not that I care, I mean, it
just normally tastes amazing.

01:05:12.761 --> 01:05:14.868
'Cause sometimes they leave
some of the fish in there

01:05:14.868 --> 01:05:16.969
and they let it cook and
it's so fucking good.

01:05:16.969 --> 01:05:19.452
But I don't know, it doesn't
feel like a proper meal.

01:05:19.452 --> 01:05:22.014
I don't know why, 'cause
I fill up so fast on sushi

01:05:22.014 --> 01:05:24.510
and then 30 minutes later
when I've left the restaurant,

01:05:24.510 --> 01:05:26.800
I'm like, "Shit, I'm hungry again."

01:05:26.800 --> 01:05:28.962
- Yeah, I get that with
sushi as well sometimes

01:05:28.962 --> 01:05:31.759
where you feel like your
stomach's about to explode,

01:05:31.759 --> 01:05:34.676
then somehow, an hour or two later,

01:05:35.818 --> 01:05:37.146
you don't get hungry.

01:05:37.146 --> 01:05:40.217
You just like, you get, you get peckish.

01:05:40.217 --> 01:05:41.727
I can eat a little more,
I can eat a little more.

01:05:41.727 --> 01:05:43.046
- I think it's just the rice that expands

01:05:43.046 --> 01:05:44.986
in your stomach.
- Probably, probably.

01:05:44.986 --> 01:05:46.705
- And then once it finally settles down,

01:05:46.705 --> 01:05:48.847
you're just like, "Oh, all
right, time for more food."

01:05:48.847 --> 01:05:49.924
- Yeah.

01:05:49.924 --> 01:05:52.788
- I don't know. I never
understood why you can eat sushi

01:05:52.788 --> 01:05:54.336
for lunch, and yet you can't eat

01:05:54.336 --> 01:05:55.827
sushi for dinner.
- Breakfast, lunch.

01:05:55.827 --> 01:05:56.706
I mean, normally-

01:05:56.706 --> 01:05:57.735
- You can eat it for breakfast!

01:05:57.735 --> 01:05:58.568
- Yeah.

01:05:58.568 --> 01:06:00.056
Normally my lunch or breakfast is sushi.

01:06:00.056 --> 01:06:01.847
- See, I can't eat sushi for breakfast.

01:06:01.847 --> 01:06:02.696
- Why not?
- I can't eat sushi

01:06:02.696 --> 01:06:03.596
for breakfast.

01:06:03.596 --> 01:06:04.767
- I can't eat fish for breakfast.

01:06:04.767 --> 01:06:05.687
- Why?

01:06:05.687 --> 01:06:06.798
- It's just weird.

01:06:06.798 --> 01:06:07.666
- But why is it weird?

01:06:07.666 --> 01:06:08.678
- You're Japanese, bro!

01:06:08.678 --> 01:06:09.511
- I know.

01:06:09.511 --> 01:06:10.719
(laughing)
I know.

01:06:10.719 --> 01:06:14.323
- Can we talk about
the Japanese breakfast?

01:06:14.323 --> 01:06:15.935
Not just the Japanese breakfast,

01:06:15.935 --> 01:06:18.133
very specifically, the-

01:06:18.133 --> 01:06:18.966
- Ryokan breakfast.

01:06:18.966 --> 01:06:19.845
- Ryokan breakfast.
- But that is

01:06:19.845 --> 01:06:20.896
the traditional Japanese breakfast.

01:06:20.896 --> 01:06:21.763
- That is the traditional
Japanese breakfast.

01:06:21.763 --> 01:06:24.173
- My first time hearing
this was Chris Broad saying,

01:06:24.173 --> 01:06:26.216
"Don't ever ask for the Japanese breakfast

01:06:26.216 --> 01:06:27.049
'cause it's shit."

01:06:27.049 --> 01:06:29.525
And I thought, oh, he's just
being pessimistic Chris.

01:06:29.525 --> 01:06:31.464
I was a fool, I should've
listened to you, Chris.

01:06:31.464 --> 01:06:32.953
It's fucking garbage!

01:06:32.953 --> 01:06:33.786
Okay, it's not.

01:06:33.786 --> 01:06:35.084
No, I think the problem is

01:06:35.084 --> 01:06:36.764
that it's the complete
opposite of garbage.

01:06:36.764 --> 01:06:38.445
It's too much, it's too good.

01:06:38.445 --> 01:06:39.707
- It's, there's like,

01:06:39.707 --> 01:06:42.410
you get about 50 different
dishes, I swear to god,

01:06:42.410 --> 01:06:44.301
And I'm just like, "Dude, it's breakfast.

01:06:44.301 --> 01:06:46.271
Just give me a bowl of the cereal."

01:06:46.271 --> 01:06:48.059
- It's like a worthy contender
with an American breakfast.

01:06:48.059 --> 01:06:50.422
Where it's just like
that's just too much food.

01:06:50.422 --> 01:06:52.580
- It's actually even more
than the American breakfast.

01:06:52.580 --> 01:06:54.610
- It's way more than
an American breakfast!

01:06:54.610 --> 01:06:57.310
Yeah, because there's,
with an American breakfast,

01:06:57.310 --> 01:06:59.690
you can fit everything on
one fucking plate, at least.

01:06:59.690 --> 01:07:01.888
With Japanese breakfast, you have like-

01:07:01.888 --> 01:07:02.721
- It covers like-

01:07:02.721 --> 01:07:04.891
- It covers this entire table.

01:07:04.891 --> 01:07:06.128
(laughing)

01:07:06.128 --> 01:07:09.381
And then as you're eating,
they bring out more dishes,

01:07:09.381 --> 01:07:12.231
more small dishes in between the fish,

01:07:12.231 --> 01:07:17.049
the tofu, the soup, the,
I can't even name it all.

01:07:17.049 --> 01:07:19.940
- There'll be like a
salad, there'll be a potato

01:07:19.940 --> 01:07:22.349
that's been marinated in
a different fucking way,

01:07:22.349 --> 01:07:23.182
I don't know.

01:07:23.182 --> 01:07:24.782
There'll be two different types of salad,

01:07:24.782 --> 01:07:27.461
probably a plate of
just single tiny things

01:07:27.461 --> 01:07:28.942
that you have no idea what the they are.

01:07:28.942 --> 01:07:30.075
They're probably gonna be radish,

01:07:30.075 --> 01:07:33.195
'cause everything seems to be radish.

01:07:33.195 --> 01:07:35.642
Like everything is a fucking
radish in these ryokans!

01:07:35.642 --> 01:07:38.581
- Every time I see a Japanese
breakfast in front of me,

01:07:38.581 --> 01:07:41.035
I'm like, "Why am I
eating an art exhibition?"

01:07:41.035 --> 01:07:42.721
That's just what it feels like.

01:07:42.721 --> 01:07:44.531
It just like this looks really pretty.

01:07:44.531 --> 01:07:46.074
It looks really pretty, but man,

01:07:46.074 --> 01:07:48.613
for one, I've never finished
a Japanese breakfast-

01:07:48.613 --> 01:07:49.921
- And then rice as well,
they give you rice.

01:07:49.921 --> 01:07:51.623
- Of course, yeah, they give you rice.

01:07:51.623 --> 01:07:54.436
This is like a five course meal

01:07:54.436 --> 01:07:56.322
that I'm having just as I've woken up,

01:07:56.322 --> 01:07:58.523
and I've never, ever
finished Japanese breakfast.

01:07:58.523 --> 01:07:59.562
- Yeah.

01:07:59.562 --> 01:08:02.183
I don't mind the fish, the cooked mackerel

01:08:02.183 --> 01:08:03.760
that they normally bring
you, I don't mind that.

01:08:03.760 --> 01:08:07.620
Mackerel doesn't really
taste like anything.

01:08:07.620 --> 01:08:08.453
- I don't know about that one.

01:08:08.453 --> 01:08:09.599
- I disagree about that.

01:08:09.599 --> 01:08:11.898
Mackerel has probably the most taste-

01:08:11.898 --> 01:08:13.337
- It's my favorite fish, mackerel,

01:08:13.337 --> 01:08:15.053
but it's just so clean.

01:08:15.053 --> 01:08:16.103
You never get any like,

01:08:16.103 --> 01:08:16.936
there's no aftertaste to mackerel,

01:08:16.936 --> 01:08:18.891
it's just a pure, it's like the chicken.

01:08:18.891 --> 01:08:20.429
- No, I get an after taste with mackerel.

01:08:20.429 --> 01:08:22.856
- Mackerel is the chicken of fish.

01:08:22.856 --> 01:08:23.889
- No, that's salmon.

01:08:23.889 --> 01:08:25.250
- That's salmon.
- Salmon!

01:08:25.250 --> 01:08:26.083
- No!

01:08:26.919 --> 01:08:28.248
- Salmon is the chicken of fish!

01:08:28.248 --> 01:08:30.089
- Salmon's the pork, salmon's the pork.

01:08:30.089 --> 01:08:31.778
- You can do so much with salmon,

01:08:31.778 --> 01:08:32.611
and people do do so.
- And that's why

01:08:32.611 --> 01:08:33.679
it's the pork!

01:08:33.679 --> 01:08:34.988
- No, that's the chicken!

01:08:34.988 --> 01:08:36.050
That's the chicken.

01:08:36.050 --> 01:08:37.670
- Mackerel's just salmon with attitude.

01:08:37.670 --> 01:08:40.331
(laughing)

01:08:40.331 --> 01:08:43.038
- Oh, I'm just recalling
all the food items

01:08:43.038 --> 01:08:43.871
they might make you.

01:08:43.871 --> 01:08:44.862
They'd probably give you eggs,

01:08:44.862 --> 01:08:47.010
but then you'd probably want fried egg,

01:08:47.010 --> 01:08:49.822
scrambled eggs, maybe a poached egg.

01:08:49.822 --> 01:08:51.530
They give you some fucking egg roll

01:08:51.530 --> 01:08:53.027
that's been rolled up and
steamed, and I'm like-

01:08:53.027 --> 01:08:54.580
- Oh, tamagoyaki?

01:08:54.580 --> 01:08:56.481
- Yeah, and it's fucking cold.

01:08:56.481 --> 01:08:57.970
And I'm like, "Why is it cold?!

01:08:57.970 --> 01:09:00.100
Give me a hot egg, please!"

01:09:00.100 --> 01:09:01.720
- Most of the dishes are actually cold.

01:09:01.720 --> 01:09:04.451
- They're all cold, and I don't
know if it's a Western thing

01:09:04.451 --> 01:09:06.091
but I want something hot to wake me up,

01:09:06.091 --> 01:09:09.461
and the worst part is you're
eating this and you're like,

01:09:09.461 --> 01:09:11.802
yeah, it's filling and
something's missing.

01:09:11.802 --> 01:09:14.442
Can I have coffee, perhaps?

01:09:14.442 --> 01:09:16.972
Do they have an espresso
machine back there, please?

01:09:16.972 --> 01:09:19.054
I bring my own pods, I don't care.

01:09:19.054 --> 01:09:21.342
Just give me a fucking coffee, please!

01:09:21.342 --> 01:09:22.856
- Well, that's what the green tea's for,

01:09:22.856 --> 01:09:24.692
it's the hot green tea.

01:09:24.692 --> 01:09:26.396
That's the hot, that's the
only heat you're gonna get

01:09:26.396 --> 01:09:27.702
out of a Japanese breakfast,

01:09:27.702 --> 01:09:29.057
Or the miso soup.

01:09:29.057 --> 01:09:30.377
- I would kill for a coffee, man,

01:09:30.377 --> 01:09:32.176
and even when we're here
with Japanese friends,

01:09:32.176 --> 01:09:34.515
sometimes they're like,
"Man, I just want a coffee."

01:09:34.515 --> 01:09:38.618
- Japanese breakfasts are way
too extra for my own liking.

01:09:38.618 --> 01:09:40.496
- [Connor And Joey] Yeah. Yeah.

01:09:40.496 --> 01:09:41.976
- But, I mean, I guess that's why

01:09:41.976 --> 01:09:44.226
it's a very infrequent occurrence.

01:09:44.226 --> 01:09:45.697
It's that special thing that you get

01:09:45.697 --> 01:09:46.847
- It's for the ryokans.
- At a ryokan.

01:09:46.847 --> 01:09:47.680
- If you go to a hotel,

01:09:47.680 --> 01:09:49.578
it's gonna be the shitty
continental breakfast

01:09:49.578 --> 01:09:50.475
that you reluctantly eat

01:09:50.475 --> 01:09:52.637
'cause you don't have
really got much choice.

01:09:52.637 --> 01:09:54.976
Oh my god, those are depressing.

01:09:54.976 --> 01:09:57.766
- I dunno, I like that
for the first two days.

