01:48:33.921 --> 01:48:35.801
or maybe I've got a shoot on Thursday,

01:48:35.801 --> 01:48:36.634
so I'm gonna eat out,

01:48:36.634 --> 01:48:38.861
So it's more like one day a week I eat in.

01:48:38.861 --> 01:48:40.533
And even then I'll just go to the combini

01:48:40.533 --> 01:48:41.961
and get the 500 Yen ramen.

01:48:41.961 --> 01:48:42.794
- Yeah.

01:48:42.794 --> 01:48:45.003
- Which is, sure, I could make my own-

01:48:45.003 --> 01:48:46.619
- Which is technically the top tier ramen.

01:48:46.619 --> 01:48:48.502
- Which I could make my own ramen.

01:48:48.502 --> 01:48:49.919
But it'd be more expensive.

01:48:49.919 --> 01:48:51.263
So it's like, yeah, of course some people,

01:48:51.263 --> 01:48:53.669
if you want to be picky about
it, yeah, you can save money.

01:48:53.669 --> 01:48:55.380
The same way if you eat pasta in the UK

01:48:55.380 --> 01:48:56.914
you'll save a shit ton of money.

01:48:56.914 --> 01:48:57.747
But if you wanna

01:48:57.747 --> 01:48:59.021
live like a human being,
- If you actually wanna

01:48:59.021 --> 01:49:00.040
enjoy your food.

01:49:00.040 --> 01:49:02.112
- Yeah, if you wanna not be depressed 24/7

01:49:02.112 --> 01:49:04.597
while you're eating, like, yeah, okay.

01:49:04.597 --> 01:49:06.662
- 'Cause going back to the combini thing

01:49:06.662 --> 01:49:08.262
about foods that we buy,

01:49:08.262 --> 01:49:11.931
I go less to the combini now to get meals.

01:49:11.931 --> 01:49:13.261
I remember when I first moved here,

01:49:13.261 --> 01:49:17.368
I would go to get a combini
meal every fucking day.

01:49:17.368 --> 01:49:20.412
And the combini fried chicken
here is fucking great.

01:49:20.412 --> 01:49:21.752
- Okay, with an asterisk.

01:49:21.752 --> 01:49:22.850
- With an asterisk.

01:49:22.850 --> 01:49:26.313
FamilyMart fried chicken
fucking sucks, okay?!

01:49:26.313 --> 01:49:27.872
It's way too greasy.

01:49:27.872 --> 01:49:30.882
- It's like a layer of like, fat.

01:49:30.882 --> 01:49:34.460
- You feel like you're eating
death as you're taking a bite.

01:49:34.460 --> 01:49:36.190
- And I see YouTubers,
I think Chris Broad says

01:49:36.190 --> 01:49:37.578
that his favorite's FamilyMart chicken

01:49:37.578 --> 01:49:38.825
and you eat into this thing,

01:49:38.825 --> 01:49:40.785
and it's the most depressed
things you can eat.

01:49:40.785 --> 01:49:41.786
- It's as depressed as he is.

01:49:41.786 --> 01:49:44.036
(laughing)

01:49:45.476 --> 01:49:47.045
- You take a bite into this thing,

01:49:47.045 --> 01:49:49.403
it is pure water and oil.

01:49:49.403 --> 01:49:52.525
That chicken was probably
anemic in its real life

01:49:52.525 --> 01:49:54.534
and they pumped that
shit with water and oil

01:49:54.534 --> 01:49:55.776
and they're like, dude do it.

01:49:55.776 --> 01:49:57.216
Lawson's fried chicken on the other hand.

01:49:57.216 --> 01:49:58.374
- Nah, nah, nah.

01:49:58.374 --> 01:50:00.883
Seven fried chicken at the top.

01:50:00.883 --> 01:50:02.300
- Seven fried chicken.
- I think Seven fried chicken

01:50:02.300 --> 01:50:03.885
is in the middle, man.

01:50:03.885 --> 01:50:06.552
Lawson's do this sweet and sour,

01:50:07.962 --> 01:50:11.646
it's salty and sweet, like
teriyaki fried chicken.

01:50:11.646 --> 01:50:13.488
It's fucking good,
dude, it's fucking good.

01:50:13.488 --> 01:50:17.516
It hits different, it
hits back. It hits back.

01:50:17.516 --> 01:50:19.496
You bite into this thing,
it's fighting you, bro,

01:50:19.496 --> 01:50:20.486
in the good way.

01:50:20.486 --> 01:50:22.132
It's like, damn, there's so
much flavor in this thing,

01:50:22.132 --> 01:50:23.694
it's like, oh shit, oh shit.

01:50:23.694 --> 01:50:24.587
(laughing)

01:50:24.587 --> 01:50:27.275
Holy shit, I just wanted the
fired chicken, not a fight.

01:50:27.275 --> 01:50:29.251
Also when you first come to Japan,

01:50:29.251 --> 01:50:31.582
you're like onigiri, bro.

01:50:31.582 --> 01:50:33.036
Jelly-filled donuts immediately.

01:50:33.036 --> 01:50:34.133
- Yeah, of course.

01:50:34.133 --> 01:50:36.885
- 'Cause it's new, it's
exciting, it tastes good.

01:50:36.885 --> 01:50:39.924
And then when I moved here,
I was eating it and I'm like,

01:50:39.924 --> 01:50:44.042
"This kind of tastes
boring, really boring."

01:50:44.042 --> 01:50:46.614
And then I thought who would
have a sandwich in Japan?

01:50:46.614 --> 01:50:49.276
I don't want a, I can get a
better sandwich in the UK.

01:50:49.276 --> 01:50:51.253
And then you start
experimenting a little bit,

01:50:51.253 --> 01:50:54.216
and I had the egg and
my go-to sandwich combo.

01:50:54.216 --> 01:50:55.917
I cry if this isn't available.

01:50:55.917 --> 01:50:58.764
In Lawson's they have a god
tier tuna mayo sandwich,

01:50:58.764 --> 01:51:01.442
and the other one is the egg one.

01:51:01.442 --> 01:51:02.454
- The egg and ham?

01:51:02.454 --> 01:51:03.933
- It's beautiful, it's beautiful, man.

01:51:03.933 --> 01:51:05.004
I cry every time I eat it.

01:51:05.004 --> 01:51:07.895
- Yeah, that is definitely my
favorite sandwich combination.

01:51:07.895 --> 01:51:09.674
- It's so good because you
have the tuna and you're like,

01:51:09.674 --> 01:51:11.985
"Ooh, a little salty, a little fishy."

01:51:11.985 --> 01:51:14.171
You have the egg and
mayo one, you're like,

01:51:14.171 --> 01:51:15.292
"Fuck, dude, this is good."

01:51:15.292 --> 01:51:16.125
- Yeah, yeah.

01:51:16.125 --> 01:51:16.958
- I'm actually the opposite.

01:51:16.958 --> 01:51:17.791
When I'm first moved here,

01:51:17.791 --> 01:51:20.405
I'm like why would I
want a fucking onigiri?

01:51:20.405 --> 01:51:23.255
And now it's just like
a very nice casual snack

01:51:23.255 --> 01:51:26.355
where you don't want a
full meal, you just want-

01:51:26.355 --> 01:51:28.102
- Onigiri's quite filling though, I find.

01:51:28.102 --> 01:51:28.993
- That's it,

01:51:28.993 --> 01:51:31.794
You have that as a snack
and it fills you up

01:51:31.794 --> 01:51:32.662
and you don't need anything else.

01:51:32.662 --> 01:51:33.568
- Yeah, exactly, exactly.

01:51:33.568 --> 01:51:35.032
- For a while.
- I guess, yeah.

01:51:35.032 --> 01:51:37.500
I always, when I go to the
combini in the morning,

01:51:37.500 --> 01:51:39.540
sometimes I can't be
bothered to make a breakfast,

01:51:39.540 --> 01:51:41.403
so I go to the combini in the morning,

01:51:41.403 --> 01:51:43.439
and I always get my breakfast

01:51:43.439 --> 01:51:45.140
and then some kind of onigiri.

01:51:45.140 --> 01:51:48.060
Because I know the breakfast
is gonna fill me up,

01:51:48.060 --> 01:51:49.928
but then I know a couple of hours later,

01:51:49.928 --> 01:51:51.906
I'm gonna be feeling a little bit peckish,

01:51:51.906 --> 01:51:53.718
And the onigiri is just perfect

01:51:53.718 --> 01:51:56.017
to fill in that little spot it creates.

01:51:56.017 --> 01:51:58.185
- My problem with onigiri is sometimes,

01:51:58.185 --> 01:52:00.368
it's like a coin toss.

01:52:00.368 --> 01:52:02.886
You might get one where they're
generous with the fillings,

01:52:02.886 --> 01:52:04.728
and sometimes you bite into that shit

01:52:04.728 --> 01:52:06.188
and there's one shred of tuna in it.

01:52:06.188 --> 01:52:07.555
And you're like, "Where's the flavor, bro?

01:52:07.555 --> 01:52:09.876
I just ate into to seaweed and rice."

01:52:09.876 --> 01:52:12.390
There was one piece of tuna
with a slap of mayo on it.

01:52:12.390 --> 01:52:13.223
- Yeah, yeah.

01:52:13.223 --> 01:52:14.497
- It sucks, man.

01:52:14.497 --> 01:52:15.949
If it was consistent, maybe I'd like it.

01:52:15.949 --> 01:52:17.870
- But you only eat the tuna onigiri.

01:52:17.870 --> 01:52:19.699
- No, I like the salmon
and the cod roe one.

01:52:19.699 --> 01:52:20.532
- Oh yeah?

01:52:20.532 --> 01:52:21.658
- Yeah, the cod roe one's fine,

01:52:21.658 --> 01:52:23.206
but cod roe is kind of intense, so.

01:52:23.206 --> 01:52:24.630
- Have you tried some
of the other flavors,

01:52:24.630 --> 01:52:27.236
like the flavored rice flavors?

01:52:27.236 --> 01:52:28.818
- Oh, you mean like the fried rice ones?

01:52:28.818 --> 01:52:30.711
The fried rice ones are fine, but again,

01:52:30.711 --> 01:52:32.150
I'm always thinking like-

01:52:32.150 --> 01:52:33.607
- They're situational for me.

01:52:33.607 --> 01:52:34.678
- I would rather them warm.

01:52:34.678 --> 01:52:36.420
(laughing)

01:52:36.420 --> 01:52:37.253
- Got back to this shit again.

01:52:37.253 --> 01:52:38.086
- I want it warm.

01:52:38.086 --> 01:52:39.854
- You can warm it up!

01:52:39.854 --> 01:52:41.366
Just put that bitch in the microwave!

01:52:41.366 --> 01:52:42.567
- It doesn't feel right.

01:52:42.567 --> 01:52:46.325
- I don't wanna microwave
rice, that's depressing, man.

01:52:46.325 --> 01:52:47.324
I don't know.

01:52:47.324 --> 01:52:48.596
- I don't know, would you rather cold rice

01:52:48.596 --> 01:52:49.637
or microwave rice?

01:52:49.637 --> 01:52:50.730
- Cold.
- Well, then stop

01:52:50.730 --> 01:52:52.512
fucking complaining (laughing).

01:52:52.512 --> 01:52:55.540
- But I would rather it be freshly-

01:52:55.540 --> 01:52:58.370
- Yeah, but that aint gonna
happen at a fucking combini.

01:52:58.370 --> 01:53:00.570
- For you, as a white person,

01:53:00.570 --> 01:53:02.262
(laughing) who grew up-

01:53:02.262 --> 01:53:03.571
- That's really situational.

01:53:03.571 --> 01:53:05.942
- As a white person.
- As a white person.

01:53:05.942 --> 01:53:07.320
- As a white person.

01:53:07.320 --> 01:53:09.368
- The point I was trying to make here

01:53:09.368 --> 01:53:12.400
is how did it feel going from eating rice

01:53:12.400 --> 01:53:15.515
every now and again to eating
rice for almost every meal?

01:53:15.515 --> 01:53:16.890
Because I've had a
conversation with people

01:53:16.890 --> 01:53:19.090
who grew up grew up in
America, grew up in England,

01:53:19.090 --> 01:53:20.260
they've moved to an Asian
country and they're like,

01:53:20.260 --> 01:53:23.697
"Man, I really it at first
and then I just got bored

01:53:23.697 --> 01:53:26.558
of eating rice for every meal."

01:53:26.558 --> 01:53:28.387
But I grew up with this
shit, so I'm used to it.

01:53:28.387 --> 01:53:29.737
- It wears you down a little bit,

01:53:29.737 --> 01:53:31.198
but I feel like you
really do get used to it.

01:53:31.198 --> 01:53:34.117
I don't know, maybe some
people, they like it at first,

01:53:34.117 --> 01:53:35.539
and, like you said, they start to hate it.

01:53:35.539 --> 01:53:37.422
But for me it was like, I don't know,

01:53:37.422 --> 01:53:39.151
rice has just always been there.

01:53:39.151 --> 01:53:41.529
It's like bread, but in a
different format for me.

01:53:41.529 --> 01:53:44.300
(laughing)

01:53:44.300 --> 01:53:46.640
It's like if bread is the hard drive,

01:53:46.640 --> 01:53:48.599
then rice is the SD card in my mind

01:53:48.599 --> 01:53:51.102
They all do the same thing.

01:53:51.102 --> 01:53:52.799
They just fill you up and they're carbs.

01:53:52.799 --> 01:53:54.129
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:53:54.129 --> 01:53:58.991
- I think most of the time
here, it's not just plain rice.

01:53:58.991 --> 01:54:01.570
Sometimes it is, like
when you go to ryokan

01:54:01.570 --> 01:54:04.140
and it's just plain fucking rice in it.

01:54:04.140 --> 01:54:06.032
And it's so starchy and
sticky, you're like,

01:54:06.032 --> 01:54:09.431
"Fuck, dude, I'm eating
fucking Play-Doh here."

01:54:09.431 --> 01:54:10.940
(laughing)

01:54:10.940 --> 01:54:14.052
But when you go to my
favorite place in the world,

01:54:14.052 --> 01:54:16.147
Matsuya, you know.

01:54:16.147 --> 01:54:17.912
- Here we go again. Here we go again.

01:54:17.912 --> 01:54:20.016
- I must look like a freak when I do this.

01:54:20.016 --> 01:54:22.616
So when they cook the pork,

01:54:22.616 --> 01:54:23.926
pork, by the way, Garnt, not beef.

01:54:23.926 --> 01:54:25.177
Beef tastes like shit.

01:54:25.177 --> 01:54:26.816
They cook the pork, right.

01:54:26.816 --> 01:54:29.613
There's like juices, and
normally you just kinda

01:54:29.613 --> 01:54:31.214
pick up the pork and put in the rice,

01:54:31.214 --> 01:54:33.077
put some mayo on it and then eat it.

01:54:33.077 --> 01:54:37.544
In the restaurant, I hold
up my plate and pour all

01:54:37.544 --> 01:54:40.333
the fats and stuff on the rice.

01:54:40.333 --> 01:54:41.854
- I know, I can agree with that.

01:54:41.854 --> 01:54:44.784
- Tastes so fucking good, dude,
'cause it makes it so rich.

01:54:44.784 --> 01:54:46.495
- But it's just the fucking the audacity

01:54:46.495 --> 01:54:50.614
to go into a beef bowl place
and order pork (laughing).

01:54:50.614 --> 01:54:51.447
- This guy.

01:54:51.447 --> 01:54:52.280
- This guy.

01:54:52.280 --> 01:54:53.410
- Honestly, you go to Matsuya, man,

01:54:53.410 --> 01:54:55.570
I'm telling you, man,
that pork and ginger.

01:54:55.570 --> 01:54:56.978
- Oh no, I've had it, it's great.

01:54:56.978 --> 01:54:58.818
- We were smashed one time and I was like-

01:54:58.818 --> 01:55:00.052
- But it's like vanilla beef.

01:55:00.052 --> 01:55:00.885
Why would I have a-

01:55:00.885 --> 01:55:02.731
- Vanilla beef! Are you out of your mind?!

01:55:02.731 --> 01:55:03.892
Don't start this again!

